      children: "CORS security vulnerabilities arise from the inherent tension between enabling legitimate cross-origin communication and maintaining the Same-Origin Policy's protective boundaries. Every CORS policy weakens default browser security, making each configuration decision a security trade-off requiring careful analysis. The vulnerabilities explored in this article-wildcard origins, origin reflection, subdomain takeover, credential leakage, null origin exploitation-all stem from insufficient rigor in this security analysis, treating CORS as a technical integration task rather than a security-critical configuration."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
